00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:30,140
 And we're going to have counts as our dictionary, so that starts out empty.

72
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:33,140
 And we're going to do a simple if then else every time through the loop.

73
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:39,140
 If the name we're looking at is not in the dictionary already, is the key, then set it to be one.

74
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:46,140
 If it's not, go get the old value, count sub name, and then add one to it and stick it back in.

75
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:50,140
 So this is, this line right here is new, adding a new thing.

76
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:54,140
 And this line right here is adding some things to existing things.

77
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:58,140
 And you do this long enough, you start with an empty one, and you do this long enough.

78
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:05,140
 At the very end, it will print out the histogram that you're looking for, the histogram you're looking for.

79
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:09,140
 And so you say, oh, we've seen CSEV twice, Zhen once, and Chen twice.

